  "notes": "The ablative is Latin's Swiss army knife, and the first question is always: IS THERE A PREPOSITION? Means, time, degree, specification and comparison go bare; accompaniment needs cum; place-from-which needs ab/dē/ex (except with city names). Manner sits in between — cum unless an adjective carries the phrase.",
